	// ⭐ **THE WHOLE-PROGRAM RE-READ OF ONE `implements` CLAUSE** — its own discriminator, and not
	// `declShapeDeclaredConformance`, because the two are mixed at DIFFERENT MOMENTS over the same declaration:
	// `recordStruct` mixes what the sweep could prove, and `refoldConformanceClause` mixes what the complete
	// index re-read. Sharing one shape would let a clause whose extent CHANGED between the two hash as a clause
	// that was read once and correctly — which is exactly the memo staleness this re-read exists to close.
