// statement (`Parser.terminateAfterDivergingCall`); one that can only ever `throw` is left by a PROPAGATING
// `try` statement and by nothing else (`Parser.desugarTry`); one whose every `return` hands back a record it
// built gives its CALLER sole ownership of that record (`Parser.emitCall`); and one that is its own
// construction is imaged by the record probe (`Parser.probedFactoryConstruction`). `foldFile` splits them
// onto their own registries at the one point the key is minted.
