	// The body's tail is a `throw` and nothing in it can return.
	leavesByThrowing

	// ⭐⭐ Every `return` in the body hands back a RECORD LITERAL or an interpolated String written in the
	// `return` itself. The record is therefore allocated by the returning frame and has had no opportunity to be referenced from
	// anywhere — there is no statement between its construction and its hand-off — so the caller adopting the
	// `+1` is that allocation's SOLE owner. See `Parser.noteFreshReturnShape` for why the shapes are exactly
	// those and nothing wider.
